==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kuu, type γ''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Kuu γ''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Kuu has great general stats for an Uber and even more towards [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies. She has great survivability and can dish out enormous damage every time she attacks. Although it may sound like her long attack rate doesn't matter that much as long as you meatshield, it can actually be a massive disadvantage in many situations. For one, she cannot reliably clear advancing peons. In the case where she misses her attack, whether it's because the boss is knocked back during the attack or she targets the frontline peons, you will have to wait about 16-18 seconds before her next attack—which is not guaranteed to hit either.

That is not to say that she's a bad general attacker, rather that she has the tendency to miss a lot and not do much.

Despite Kuu being [[Strong Against]] Dark enemies, they are rarely a good matchup because of the tendency of Dark enemies to have many knockbacks. However, Kuu still does a great job against the few exceptions such as [[Chocolate Doge]], [[Razorback]] and [[Dark Otter]]. Red enemies are better as they tend to have few knockbacks anyway, but she is still a risky matchup against them due to Reds being just as aggressive as Darks.

==='''True Form'''===
Divine Kuu γ gains more health, increased attack power, a quicker attack rate and more range in True Form. Unfortunately, they are not improved significantly enough to realistically change her effect in battle, so the best thing that can be gained out of her True Form is her higher range. Notably, her health is increased almost twofold, but that does not matter widely otherwise.

==='''Talents'''===
Unlocking her '''[[Weaken]]''' and leaving it at level one could be argued to be worth the cost, but it should only be considered if you're intending on investing into her Ultra Talents. '''Attack Buff''' and '''Defense Buff''' are better options, as they directly improve this unit's performance on the battlefield, be sure to invest into her with Catseyes first though. '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Waves]]''' does very little for the extreme investment. '''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]]''' should be saved for when you get Kuu's Ultra Talents, as Curse Immunity and Target Relic go hand in hand.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
This is where things start to head in a much more positive direction.

'''Attack Frequency Up''' is Kuu's much needed redemption. This takes her cumbersome attack rate and narrows it down significantly. Now, she attacks every 8.63 seconds, a massive improvement over her original attack rate. With this, Kuu now proves herself incredibly powerful as a nuker, and can compare incredibly nicely to her peers.

At Lv.60 with max Attack Buff Talents, Kuu has a DPS of 20.9k against untargeted traits (37,600 against Red/Dark), which is good enough to justify the purchase. While the Red nuker niche is quite oversaturated as is, she makes up for it by providing immensely powerful generalist value on top of her existing uses. Her niche as an anti-Dark is also much better, since her attack rate is enough for her to not be immediately overwhelmed.

Additionally, Kuu can now '''Target Relic''', and pairing it with her Decrease TBA talent turns her into a Relic slaughterer very comparable to [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]]. Because of this, Kuu can easily take down most Relic enemies with complete ease, and if she doesn't, she still helps by doing powerful chip damage. While Luza has the advantage of piercing on his second hit, {{4c}} usage, Behemoth Slayer, and some extra immunities, Kuu is superior in terms of raw stats thanks to not relying on her abilities as much.

To top everything off, Kuu also gets '''[[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]]''', which has quite a few uses, notably for countering [[Red EnerG]], [[Raynard]], [[Ancient Magamojoe]] and the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]] in terms of pure niche performance. Most of these enemies aren't prominent and all have their own counters, but Kuu can help tremendously if you lack Surge Immune attackers.

Note that Kuu isn't that strong of an Uber without a majority of these Ultra Talents, which can make the large investment a lot less appealing. It's also worth keeping in mind that many powerful anti-Relic options exist in the endgame, such as the aforementioned Ape Lord Luza, which can render this investment redundant if you're already satisfied with their performance. Nonetheless, her impeccable performance in many situations makes her the bane of all Red/Dark/Relic in her range.

