==Trivia==
*She was added to the game alongside [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai]] and [[Coppermine (Uber Rare Cat)|Coppermine]] on May 14th, 2014.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Kuu was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Journey to the West (Removed Combo)|Journey to the West]].
*Divine Kuu γ gained [[Immune to Weaken]] in [[Version 5.3 Update|Version 5.3]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], Kuu's True Form's name lacked the "γ" part in BCEN.
**The original name can still be seen in an outdated screenshot used in the help section for extra [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]] slots
*She was one of the first units to receive Ultra Talents, alongside [[Megidora (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Megidora]] and [[Akira (Uber Rare Cat)|Inferno Akira]].
*Kuu is based on [[wikipedia:Sun Wukong|Sun Wukong/Monkey King]] from ''[[wikipedia:Journey to the West|Journey to the West]]'' - the Bo/Staff and the cloud riding are common traits in Wukong's portrayal.
*Kuu and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] seem to be on poor terms with each other. [[Jungle Women (Combo)|Jungle Women]]'s Japanese name, Ken'en no Naka (犬猿の仲), literally translates to "Dog-monkey Relationship" and refers to a contentious relationship characterized by mutual hatred or extremely poor relations, like the rivalry between dogs and monkeys. Kuu fills the "monkey" role because she's based on Sun Wukong.
*[[Adventurer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Fabled Adventure Girl Kanna]]'s design is likely based on that of Kuu; Their outfits include the same general features, both of them stand on floating platforms to hover above the ground, and their attacks both involve objects crashing down onto enemies in front of them.

